Data license for `data/`
========================

Copyright (c) 2026 AIVALIX Inc. and Indigo Corporation

The files in this directory that are **this project's own contributions** are
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0):

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Every dataset in `data/` originates from a third-party source. This license
covers only the work added here on top of those sources — the reconstructed
gold answer sets, the entity grounding and correction tables, the query-pattern
classification, and the format conversions. It does **not** and cannot
re-license the upstream data itself, which remains governed by its own terms.
`THIRD_PARTY_DATA.md` in this directory lists every upstream source, its
license, and the modifications made here.


Scope
-----

CC BY 4.0, original contributions of this project:

    pcqa/qa/eval_v2.jsonl          Entity-set gold, 241 questions
    pcqa/qa/eval_v2_clean.jsonl    Entity-set gold after the type-consistency
                                   audit, 205 questions (the PcQA benchmark
                                   reported in the paper)
    pcqa/qa/eval_v3.jsonl          Entity-set gold, earlier 352-question build
    pcqa/entity_mappings.json      Seed-entity to KG-node grounding map
    pcqa/manual_entity_fixes.json  Manual synonym / spelling corrections
    pcqa/sample_categories.json    17 (anchor, target-type) query patterns

CC BY 4.0 as a derived adaptation; the upstream license also applies and the
modification is recorded in `THIRD_PARTY_DATA.md`:

    metaqa/import_nodes.csv        Neo4j-import conversion of MetaQA
    metaqa/import_rels.csv
    metaqa/qa/*.jsonl              Evaluation-format conversion of MetaQA
    pcqa/import_nodes.csv          Neo4j-import conversion of the public
    pcqa/import_rels.csv           subset of the KGT pan-cancer graph
    primekgqa/import_nodes.csv     Neo4j-import conversion of PrimeKG nodes

Not covered by this license:

    pcqa/PcQA.json                 Redistributed from the KGT release (CC0 1.0)
    pcqa/README.md                 Describes the upstream KGT graph build
    pcqa/build_eval_cypher.py      Source code — MIT, see the repository root


Attribution
-----------

When reusing the CC BY 4.0 material above, please credit:

    Kotaro Oshima and Yoichi Takahashi.
    "Grounding Extended Type-KoPL with KG-Structure Feedback:
     Anchor-Probe Feedback and Cypher-Informed Reranking."
    KGE-LLM 2026 Workshop at IJCKG 2026. CEUR Workshop Proceedings.
    https://github.com/AIVALIX/Extended_Type_KoPL

and indicate whether you modified the material. Reuse of the underlying
datasets additionally requires the attribution demanded by their own licenses
(MetaQA in particular is CC BY 3.0 and requires both attribution and a notice
of modification).


No warranty
-----------

The data is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The reconstructed
PcQA gold answer sets were produced by an LLM classifier with manual review and
a type-consistency audit, as described in the paper; residual annotation errors
are possible.
